<!--

1. PRIORITY SCORING:
   - 1.0 = Homepage (most important)
   - 0.9 = High-traffic pages (main methods)
   - 0.7 = Medium-traffic pages
   - 0.5 = Lower-traffic pages
   - 0.3 = Legal/meta pages
   
   NOTE: Priority is relative WITHIN your site only
              It does NOT guarantee better ranking overall

2. CHANGEFREQ GUIDE:
   - always: Updates multiple times per day
   - hourly: Major news/real-time data
   - daily: Frequently updated content
   - weekly: Regular content updates
   - monthly: Seasonal/periodic updates
   - yearly: Wikipedia-style articles
   - never: Static/archived content
   
   TIP: Google ignores this value; use it only as a hint

3. LASTMOD (Last Modified Date):
   - IMPORTANT for ranking "fresh" content
   - Only include if you actually update the page
   - Google weights recent updates more heavily
   - Must be in ISO 8601 format: YYYY-MM-DD
   
   SEO BENEFIT: Pages with recent lastmod = 10-20% higher ranking

4. HREFLANG (Language/Region Alternatives):
   - Tells Google about language versions
   - Prevents duplicate content penalties
   - Lets Google show right version per locale
   - CRITICAL for international SEO
   
   EXAMPLE:
   <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="..."/>
   <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="uz" href="..."/>
   <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="..."/>

5. SITEMAP SIZE LIMITS:
   - Max 50,000 URLs per file
   - Max 50 MB uncompressed
   - If you exceed: Create multiple sitemaps
   
   EXAMPLE FOR LARGE SITES:
   sitemap-1.xml (URLs 1-50,000)
   sitemap-2.xml (URLs 50,001-100,000)
   sitemap-index.xml (references both)

6. IMAGE SITEMAPS (if needed):
   Use <image:image> tags for important images
   Helps Google index and rank images properly
   
   EXAMPLE:
   <image:image>
     <image:loc>https://sonli-usullar.uz/image.jpg</image:loc>
     <image:title>Method Visualization</image:title>
   </image:image>

7. NEWS SITEMAPS (if you publish articles):
   Use <news:news> tags for recent articles
   Helps Google News index content faster
   
   EXAMPLE:
   <news:news>
     <news:publication>
       <news:name>Sonli Usullar Blog</news:name>
       <news:language>en</news:language>
     </news:publication>
     <news:publication_date>2026-04-02</news:publication_date>
     <news:title>Article Title</news:title>
   </news:news>

8. TESTING & SUBMISSION:
   a) Validate XML: Go to https://xmlsitemaps.com/validate-xml-sitemap.html
   
   b) Submit to Google Search Console:
      - Settings › Sitemaps › Add Sitemap
      - Paste: https://sonli-usullar.uz/sitemap.xml
   
   c) Submit to Bing Webmaster Tools:
      - https://www.bing.com/webmasters/tools/
   
   d) Monitor in GSC:
      - Sitemaps › Sitemap Report
      - Check: Submitted, Discovered, Indexed counts

9. AUTOMATIC SITEMAP GENERATION:
   For WordPress: Use Yoast SEO, Rank Math, or All in One SEO
   For Static Sites: Use screaming-frog.com (free version)
   For Node.js: Use sitemap npm package
   For Python: Use sitemap library

10. COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID:
    ❌ URLs not matching actual pages (404 errors)
    ❌ Including canonicalized/noindexed pages
    ❌ Incorrect date format (not ISO 8601)
    ❌ Too many URLs (50K+ in single file)
    ❌ Not submitting to Google Search Console
    ❌ Not updating lastmod when pages change
    ❌ Including parameters in URLs (session IDs, etc.)

11. MONITORING:
    Check Google Search Console WEEKLY:
    - Requested Indexing: Have pages been crawled?
    - Coverage: How many pages indexed?
    - Enhancements: Any structured data issues?
    
    Optimal metrics:
    ✅ Submitted = Indexed (100% coverage desired)
    ✅ No crawl errors
    ✅ No enhanced content issues

-->

